 "sayLines": [
  {
   "day": 10,
   "text": "◈ FLASHBACK — Aisha's Drawing\nKitchen table, burnt pancakes. You told her the sun needed holding, and she took you literally — drew you carrying it with both hands. She was six. The sky changed three weeks later."
  },
  {
   "day": 24,
   "text": "\"Your understanding is... deepening! We can see it! Like watching a seed decide to be a tree! Beautiful! Profitable!\""
  },
  {
   "day": 25,
   "text": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Fernando speaks at Emberhold's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 26,
   "text": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Fernando speaks at Thornfield's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 27,
   "text": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Fernando speaks at Ashford's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 27,
   "text": "Three fires bow to Haven. But a realm isn't leverage — it's seasons. These bonds are young; tend them, keep the trust, and the court will come."
  },
  {
   "day": 32,
   "text": "💔 A faction of Stonebridge has turned cannibal — and split. The eaters walked. The Red Table is a new fire in the world now — 2 people under Kira."
  },
  {
   "day": 32,
   "text": "📓 Codex: Stonebridge split (cannibal). The Red Table formed; 2 petition at Haven's fire."
  },
  {
   "day": 35,
   "text": "Word later: they walked to The Red Table. Another fire in the world, whether you wanted it or not."
  },
  {
   "day": 38,
   "text": "✨ Ability gained: Fusion Reactor (L1). The System installs your fusion pellet — properly, inside you. You never need to eat again: the pellet covers your metabolism, and your strikes and abilities burn with a steady reactor fire (1.25x, always on). One reactor per world, and it never comes out: not unslotted, not un-taught, not surrendered. Death is the only uninstall. But the hunger is gone, and "
  },
  {
   "day": 42,
   "text": "🧳 A traveler passed through yesterday, talking about a village to the southeast called The Red Table. The region is bigger than your fire."
  },
  {
   "day": 47,
   "text": "🧳 Word comes late, through traders: The Hungry Road and The Red Table have bound together — The Hungry Road primary. Other fires are climbing, too."
  },
  {
   "day": 47,
   "text": "📓 Codex: The Hungry Road and The Red Table bound; The Hungry Road primary."
  },
  {
   "day": 48,
   "text": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
  },
  {
   "day": 52,
   "text": "🥣 Tomás of The Red Table walks into your firelight alone, thinner than you remember. \"Our jars are empty,\" they say. No preamble. \"I'm asking for food.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 54,
   "text": "Tomás waits two days at your fire, getting thinner. Nobody answers. They walk back to The Red Table with nothing. They'll remember the silence."
  },
  {
   "day": 60,
   "text": "A runner from The Red Table, dusty and direct: \"Your foragers are stripping our side of the southeast ground. Back off — or we'll talk with teeth.\" (Trust -3. The commons cuts both ways.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 74,
   "text": "🥣 Tomás of The Red Table walks into your firelight alone, thinner than you remember. \"Our jars are empty,\" they say. No preamble. \"I'm asking for food.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 76,
   "text": "◈ SYSTEM: \"Four fires. One head. GOVERNANCE LAYER: online — polity tribute routing, the court calendar, famine reserves. You built a realm. Try not to lose it the way you found it.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 76,
   "text": "📓 Codex: National beat staged: lead (4 villages)."
  },
  {
   "day": 76,
   "text": "Tomás waits two days at your fire, getting thinner. Nobody answers. They walk back to The Red Table with nothing. They'll remember the silence."
  },
  {
   "day": 77,
   "text": "🍲 The shared granary opens: 5,000 kcal for every fire of the realm, no strings. Emberhold, Thornfield, Ashford count it — and remember who fed them first. (Trust +10 with each.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 77,
   "text": "◈ SYSTEM: \"Oh. OH. Do you feel that? That's the whole PLANET leaning in. ...There's a table, little fires. A big one. Far away. And it is LOOKING at you. Give it a season worth judging.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 89,
   "text": "📓 Codex: you've heard of **Harvest Table**. Someone, somewhere, can do this. Now you know its name."
  },
  {
   "day": 89,
   "text": "◈ THE SYSTEM has been watching Milagros — Combat 1. Three offers; they took Harvest Table. Earned, chosen. (harvest_table: villager level-up)"
  },
  {
   "day": 89,
   "text": "📓 Codex: Milagros chose Harvest Table (harvest_table) at Combat 1."
  },
  {
   "day": 90,
   "text": "◈ THE TABLE — the ring of pale light flickers at the edge of the sky... and does not come. The System does not apologize this time. \"WE PRICED THE RUN. NO HUNGER ON THE RECORD — THE PELLET HUMS WHERE THE FIRE SHOULD BE. NO FEAST, NO SURGE, NOTHING HERE WE CAN PRICE. A COLD SPOT AT EVERY TABLE: THE WORDS WERE ON THE WRAPPER.\" The ledger still wants: the food-thesis deeds (no feast can carry the sur"
  },
  {
   "day": 96,
   "text": "🥣 Tomás of The Red Table walks into your firelight alone, thinner than you remember. \"Our jars are empty,\" they say. No preamble. \"I'm asking for food.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 98,
   "text": "Tomás waits two days at your fire, getting thinner. Nobody answers. They walk back to The Red Table with nothing. They'll remember the silence."
  },
  {
   "day": 105,
   "text": "🧳 Word from The Red Table: Marcus is dead, and Grace and Cole both claim the fire. The Red Table is choosing — or fighting."
  },
  {
   "day": 108,
   "text": "◈ WORD TRAVELS — riders from The Red Table bring talk of Haven. Out there they call you the Feared. The show's narration lingers on your hands."
  },
  {
   "day": 111,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They carried off ~800 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 114,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They carried off ~672 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 119,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They carried off ~1140 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 128,
   "text": "You caught the lie in his face and watched the whole table react to it before he'd finished the sentence. Face and room, both open books."
  },
  {
   "day": 130,
   "text": "🌙 Night. Shouts from the treeline — Kira of The Red Table with 3 others, and they're not here to talk. \"Your pantry or your blood. Choose.\" (They want ~2,000 kcal.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 131,
   "text": "🌙 You weren't at the treeline. Kira of The Red Table didn't wait — they hit the stores and melted back into the dark with 803 kcal. The village will talk about this for a long time."
  },
  {
   "day": 136,
   "text": "🌙 The cookfire's smell carried further than the laughter did — smoke and grease on the night wind. Big Loud is circling the edge of the light. It followed the feast here. (A scavenger, drawn by the feast. Face it while the feast is in you — or let the watch drive it off.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 136,
   "text": "🔥 Caitlin takes up a brand and Keerthi follows — they meet it at the edge of the light with noise and fire. Big Loud was never brave. It melts back into the dark. (The watch drove off the feast's scavenger. The devotion stays armed; the feast's fire still burns in you.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 144,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They carried off ~1301 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 145,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They carried off ~600 kcal from the pantry. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 148,
   "text": "\"Your understanding is... deepening! We can see it! Like watching a seed decide to be a tree! Beautiful! Profitable!\""
  },
  {
   "day": 163,
   "text": "🌙 Raid — The Red Table came in the night from the southeast. They trampled 2 garden plots into mud. Nobody's dead, but the message is clear: the ground is theirs too, and they're done asking. (Trust -10.)"
  },
  {
   "day": 169,
   "text": "🪞 You wake up somebody else. Milagros Piazza, 42 — an ER nurse. Their hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Beard Moss, Loud Chewer, Harvest Table, Pyrokinesis, Green Thumb, Literally."
  },
  {
   "day": 169,
   "text": "🥣 Tomás of The Red Table walks into your firelight alone, thinner than you remember. \"Our jars are empty,\" they say. No preamble. \"I'm asking for food.\""
  }
